{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: the code was compiled to SPIR-V with glslangValidator\n  optimized with spirv-opt -O (what follows is beyond that)\nexec of SPIR-V (43 instructions), entry main, 4 lanes in lockstep, cost model gt1030\n  buffers start with random values (seed 1)\n  input 1 = img (binding 0): ramp8.png RGBA8 8x8, mipmapped, checksum 4fc70659\n  note: uv (location 0) is taken as the pixel's uv: its centre over the image size, 0..1\n  the trace: lanes at pixels (4,4)..(5,5) of the 8x8 image\n  output o: RGBA8 8x8, checksum 7abe74ad\n  sampling: linear filtering, linear mips, repeat (the sampler's state is not in SPIR-V: assumed; say `sampler nearest clamp`, or `input 1 nearest mirror`); implicit LOD from the quad's fine derivatives, mips by a 2x2 box filter, filter weights in double precision\n  serial form:\n    %15 = OpLoad %12 %img                        load       6.875  t = 0..6.875  -> tex1+smp1 tex1+smp1 tex1+smp1 tex1+smp1\n    %19 = OpLoad %v2float %uv                                   0  t = 6.875..6.875  -> (0.5625,0.5625) (0.6875,0.5625) (0.5625,0.6875) (0.6875,0.6875)\n    %20 = OpImageSampleImplicitLod %v4float %15 %19 tex_sample 21.625  t = 6.875..28.5  -> (0.50196,0.50196,0.7490 (0.62745,0.50196,0.6862 (0.50196,0.62745,0.7490 (0.62745,0.62745,0.6862\n    %21 = OpVectorShuffle %v4float %20 %20 2 1 0 3                0  t = 28.5..28.5  -> (0.74902,0.50196,0.5019 (0.68627,0.50196,0.6274 (0.74902,0.62745,0.5019 (0.68627,0.62745,0.6274\n    OpStore %o %21                                              0  t = 28.5..28.5\n  time 28.5 for every lane; lanes busy 100% (0 lane-units idle: masked, or waiting for an atomic)\n  animation: 650x466, 225 frames at 30 fps (6.0 s, then the result for 1.5 s), 1 s = 4.8 cost units; 91811 bytes\n  (nofile: GIF checksum 165d8cac)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "animate", "ucas": "animate exec input 1 gallery 1 seed 1 nofile", "structure